  "result": "I wrote the O3 quiz, `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key in `keys/0002.json`. It has six items, four multiple-choice and two numeric, and every item is on O3.\n\nThe quiz is ahead of the lessons, because no lesson exists yet for O3. I built the content from the objective's wording, `MISSION.md` and `NOTES.md`.\n\nIt covers:\n- what one column means: the endpoint's linear and angular velocity when only that joint moves;\n- the moment arm running all the way to the endpoint;\n- the axis written in base coordinates, which depends on the earlier joints;\n- a rotary column's angular part;\n- a prismatic column's linear and angular parts;\n- how moving the endpoint changes the matrix.\n\nTwo review passes ran. I fixed the second pass's six findings in a last version, which was not reviewed again because of the two-pass cap. I declined one of them, splitting the shared misconception id on two prismatic-column options, and the record explains why. The record is `review-records/0002-quiz.md`.\n\nThe review drafts are in `drafts/`.",
